Overlay patch 0030: thread-safe CVar map (reference 0030 ported;
Sync Wave 2 item 1 — CRITICAL). reference device crashes: SIGSEGV on the
audio thread's CVarGetInteger while the main thread wrote CVars (death,
pause) — mVariables is a bare unordered_map; a concurrent insert can
rehash while the reader is inside find() -> freed-bucket deref.
GHOSTSHIP HAS THE SAME ARCHITECTURE: HandleAudioThread reads
gSettings.Volume.Master every synth update (src/port/Engine.cpp) while
the main thread writes CVars. Fix: recursive_mutex over every mVariables
access. Reads funnel through Get(); writes are the five Set*,
ClearVariable, CopyVariable, Save (iteration), Load (clear).
FORK COVERAGE CHECK (per the wave doc's assert-your-fork warning): this
fork's extra ClearBlock has no direct map access (delegates to Load,
covered); LoadFromPath/LoadLegacy write only via Set* under Load's lock
(recursive). Residual as reference: GetString's char* after a concurrent
SetString free — no audio-thread string reads exist here either.

